{"id":"resp_883a779febba1629","created_at":1795618463,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_83d72d0670571fb2","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to output revised SHACL code that addresses the technical representation error.\n\nCurrent SHACL defines two property constraints:\n\n- constructionContractDate with date range.\n- applicableIceClassRegulationEdition with sh:hasValue iceClassRegulationEdition2010.\n\nIssue: conditional relationship—applicableIceClassRegulationEdition should be required only when constructionContractDate falls within the range.\n\nWe need to replace unconditional block with conditional shape.\n\nWe must not delete constraints unless supported, but this is needed.\n\nWe can implement using sh:or with two shapes: one shape for ships that meet date range (with edition constraint), another shape with no edition constraint (i.e., no constraint). Or use sh:if...sh:then with SHACL-SPARQL? SHACL core doesn't have sh:if then but there is sh:property with sh:or? Actually we can use sh:or on node shape level: combine two node shapes: a node shape that checks date range and then edition; and a node shape that checks date not in range (so no edition). But we need to ensure that if date falls within range, edition must be the 2010 edition; otherwise, edition can be anything.\n\nSimpler: use sh:or with two sh:property constraints? No, with sh:or we can specify alternative sets of constraints. We'll declare two shapes:\n\nvocab:ShipIceClass2010Shape (existing) stays but we modify. Perhaps create a new shape that includes sh:or with two shapes defined via sh:node? Actually we can embed sh:or directly in the node shape using sh:or with list of shapes (blank node). For each alternative, we define constraints.\n\nAlternative 1: date in range AND edition = 2010.\n\nAlternative 2: date not in range (so either < min or >= max) — no edition constraint (or maybe we could ignore edition). Could be just a shape with date constraint only.\n\nBut we already have date constraint defined as a property shape. Using sh:or we would duplicate date constraint? Might be okay.\n\nBetter: Use sh:property with sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate and then a sh:or at property level? Not possible.\n\nWe'll restructure:\n\nvocab:ShipIceClass2010Shape a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    sh:or (\n        [   # Case when date in range, require edition 2010\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:message \"Construction contract date must be between ...\" ;\n            ] ;\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:applicableIceClassRegulationEdition ;\n                sh:hasValue vocab:iceClassRegulationEdition2010 ;\n                sh:message \"Ships built ... must have applicableIceClassRegulationEdition set to iceClassRegulationEdition2010.\" ;\n            ]\n        ]\n        [   # Case when date not in range, no edition constraint\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                # We need to assert that date is NOT in the range.\n                # Use sh:not with a property shape? There's sh:not to invert constraints at node shape level, but for property we can use sh:property with sh:or? Actually we can use sh:property with sh:or with a shape that enforces date not in range? Possibly use sh:or with sh:property having sh:maxInclusive \"2012-01-01\" and sh:minInclusive \"2019-01-01\"? Hmm.\n\nSimpler: Use sh:or with two node shape alternatives:\n\nAlternative A: (date in range AND edition 2010). This includes both constraints as above.\n\nAlternative B: (date not in range). We can express using sh:not with a shape that enforces date in range. For Alternative B we can just say sh:not [ sh:property [ sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ; sh:datatype xsd:date ; sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ; sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ] ] . That ensures date is not within range, but still we may want any date? If date is missing? Could be fine.\n\nThus final shape: sh:or ( list of two alternative NodeShape definitions ).\n\nLet's produce code with proper prefixes and RDF list syntax using parentheses.\n\nNeed to include complete shape block.\n\nMake sure to preserve existing prefixes.\n\nProvide revised SHACL.\n\nWill include comment.\n\nLet's craft:\n\nvocab:ShipIceClass2010Shape a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    sh:or (\n        [   # ship with date in 2012-01-01 inclusive to 2019-01-01 exclusive must have edition 2010\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:message \"Construction contract date must be between 2012‑01‑01 (inclusive) and 2019‑01‑01 (exclusive) for applicability of the 2010 Ice Class Regulations.\" ;\n            ] ;\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:applicableIceClassRegulationEdition ;\n                sh:hasValue vocab:iceClassRegulationEdition2010 ;\n                sh:message \"Ships built under the 2010 Ice Class Regulations must have applicableIceClassRegulationEdition set to iceClassRegulationEdition2010.\" ;\n            ]\n        ]\n        [   # ship with constructionContractDate outside that interval – no edition constraint\n            sh:not [\n                sh:property [\n                    sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                    sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                    sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                    sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                ]\n            ]\n        ]\n    ) .\n\nMake sure to close shape.\n\nThat's the revised shape.\n\nWe also need to keep other parts unchanged, but there were no other parts.\n\nThus produce final block.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_a3f9f2c19054b393","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix vocab: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape for ships where the 2010 ice‑class edition applies only when the construction contract date\n# falls between 2012‑01‑01 (inclusive) and 2019‑01‑01 (exclusive).  If the date is outside this interval,\n# no restriction on the applicableIceClassRegulationEdition is imposed.\nvocab:ShipIceClass2010Shape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass vocab:ship ;\n    sh:or (\n        # ---- CASE 1: Date within the 2010‑edition interval → edition must be 2010\n        [\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                sh:message \"Construction contract date must be between 2012‑01‑01 (inclusive) and 2019‑01‑01 (exclusive) for applicability of the 2010 Ice Class Regulations.\" ;\n            ] ;\n            sh:property [\n                sh:path vocab:applicableIceClassRegulationEdition ;\n                sh:hasValue vocab:iceClassRegulationEdition2010 ;\n                sh:message \"Ships built under the 2010 Ice Class Regulations must have applicableIceClassRegulationEdition set to iceClassRegulationEdition2010.\" ;\n            ]\n        ]\n        # ---- CASE 2: Date NOT within the interval → no edition constraint\n        [\n            sh:not [\n                sh:property [\n                    sh:path vocab:constructionContractDate ;\n                    sh:datatype xsd:date ;\n                    sh:minInclusive \"2012-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                    sh:maxExclusive \"2019-01-01\"^^xsd:date ;\n                ]\n            ]\n        ]\n    ) .\n</END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":83258,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":320,"cache_write_tokens":82928,"input_tokens_per_turn":[83258],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[320]},"output_tokens":1865,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1344,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1865],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":85123},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}